.TH CDCSTORE-RESTORE 1 "October 2026" "cdcstore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cdcstore\-restore \- restore files from a cdcstore repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdcstore\-restore
[\-o OUTDIR] [\-f] [\-q] REPO [PATTERN...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restores files from a repository. REPO is the repository folder, or a folder that holds .cdcstore (as cdcstore\-add \-X makes). With no PATTERN everything is restored. A PATTERN is a path (a file, or a folder with everything in it) or a wildcard (* ? [..]) matched against the stored path; a wildcard also takes in what is below a matching folder. Quote wildcards so the shell leaves them alone.
.PP
Files are written under OUTDIR with their stored paths, modes and times. Every chunk file of the restored files must be present.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o DIR
Restore under DIR (default: the current folder; made if missing).
.TP
.B \-f
Overwrite files that already exist. Otherwise they are skipped and reported.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet.
.TP
.B \-h
Print help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
cdcstore\-restore \-o out REPO
cdcstore\-restore \-o out REPO 'GAMES/DOOM*' '*.EXE'
.RE
.fi
.sp
